src/staking/AbstractStakingStrategy.sol:convertToAssets:51|class=C15|High|An unprivileged actor drives a position into the "partially escrowed" state — by liquidating part of it (_postLiquidation tokenizes and carves out part of the withdraw request while _isWithdrawRequestPending stays true) or by partially redeeming through the escrowed _redeemShares path — after which convertToAssets early-returns the manager's escrow-only value for the entire shares argument, forwarding an unclamped shares that no longer matches w.sharesAmount, so the position is priced either by linear extrapolation of a shrunken escrow claim (reads richer than assets actually held → over-borrow against the vault) or by discarding the still-vault-held PT remainder (reads poorer → force-liquidate a third party at a price the vault's own balance contradicts).|src/staking/AbstractStakingStrategy.sol
